the function will work properly.  BUG=None TEST=manual  Change-Id: I8f32204d14f2e25553a544f8f3575b60ee21c59c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/547164 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="547164" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/64/547164/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6442943bee7339fedbe7cc917032c2d376c2c6c5" commit="ee24a7baa5d6db5ae14514ade410663d4c096ab7" commit_message="Servo: EC: Add volume button controls  Volume up/ down buttons will be used in new FW menu UI to select menu items. Adding the drivers to poppy overlay.  BUG=b:36636462 TEST= Firmware EC tests pass  Change-Id: I6442943bee7339fedbe7cc917032c2d376c2c6c5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/530529 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="530529" owner_email="gkihumba@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" ref="refs/changes/29/530529/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3d2964a79e710428f7a6e7004d68ab424af85be8" commit="267b7477359109a85f5a7ad25c25221325ca64ce" commit_message="tcpm: add .release driver operation.  similar to the USB_PD_TCPC case, add release/init operations when the pd_task enters/leaves the PD_STATE_SUSPENDED state.  one use case for PD_SUSPEND is to get exlusive access to the TCPC for things like firmware update, so the release/init operation is needed to get the TCPC and driver into a good state.  updated all tcpm_drv style drivers.  for backward compatibility, &quot;old&quot; drivers that may not handle init/release properly simply return EC_ERROR_UNIMPLEMENTED for tcpm_release().  pd_task() uses this as a signal that it should not try to re-init() the driver.  TEST=tested in combination with follow-on CLs to do TCPC firmware  update on electro.  also built for kevin, eve, sand which are  some of the other boards using these drivers.  &quot;make buildall -j&quot; passes.  BRANCH=none  BUG=b:35586896  Change-Id: I3d2964a79e710428f7a6e7004d68ab424af85be8 Signed-off-by: Caveh Jalali &lt;caveh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/544660 Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="544660" owner_email="caveh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/60/544660/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="9695.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>